        "sourceText": "# Paddle Star\n\nTime limit: $1$ second. Memory limit: $1024$ MiB. Standard input and standard output.\n\nPutata has recently become fascinated with playing Zoe. He is practicing her ability, Paddle Star.\n\nZoe fires a star and can redirect it during flight. The damage increases with the flying distance. Suppose she is at point $X$ and fires in any direction. If she redirects the star at point $Y$ toward point $Z$, its path is $X\\to Y\\to Z$. If the star meets an enemy anywhere on its path, it disappears immediately and damages that enemy.\n\nPutata is not skilled enough to control the ability freely. The first segment $XY$ always has length $\\ell_1$, and the second segment $YZ$ always has length $\\ell_2$. Zoe faces a fixed direction $\\overrightarrow{XP}$. Let the directed angle from $\\overrightarrow{XP}$ to $\\overrightarrow{XY}$ be $\\theta$ degrees, and the directed angle from $\\overrightarrow{XY}$ to $\\overrightarrow{YZ}$ be $\\varphi$ degrees. They satisfy $\\theta\\in[-\\alpha,\\alpha]$ and $\\varphi\\in[-\\beta,\\beta]$.\n\n![diagram](paddle-star-diagram.png)\n\nPutata's rival Budada wants to know the total area that could possibly be attacked by Putata's Zoe. Budada is busy with mathematics, so help him find it.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains the number of test cases $T$ ($1\\leq T\\leq 10^5$).\n\nEach test case consists of one line containing four integers $\\ell_1,\\ell_2,\\alpha,\\beta$ ($1\\leq\\ell_2\\leq\\ell_1\\leq 10^9$, $0\\leq\\alpha\\leq90$, $0\\leq\\beta<180$), describing the ability.\n\n## Output\n\nFor each test case, output one real number: the total area. The absolute or relative error must not exceed $10^{-6}$.\n\nFormally, if your answer is $a$ and the jury's answer is $b$, it is accepted when\n\n$$\n\\frac{|a-b|}{\\max(1,|b|)}\\leq10^{-6}.\n$$\n",
